    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
    "body": "For those that use `mini.files`, are your icons using the single width variant instead of the double width variant? I looked in the source code and there is a space appended when the icon is selected, so I'm not sure why my terminal (wezterm) is not rendering the double width icon. As you can see in the screenshot, it **does** render the double width icon in the tabline, so I'm not really sure what is going on here.\r\n<img width=\"1017\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0eaaf2c7-a0cf-487c-9d6a-09a58e6a3621\">\r\n\r\nAnd then I fired up Kitty to see what happens there. It does render the double width icons in `mini.files`, but `mini.tabline` oddly renders the **active** tab with the single width icon. As I switch between buffers, the active buffer's icons shrinks. Here is a video:\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/17c11b19-921a-45ca-adc4-29d9df8dcbd4\r\n",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">For those that use <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.files</code>, are your icons using the single width variant instead of the double width variant? I looked in the source code and there is a space appended when the icon is selected, so I'm not sure why my terminal (wezterm) is not rendering the double width icon. As you can see in the screenshot, it <strong>does</strong> render the double width icon in the tabline, so I'm not really sure what is going on here.<br>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/747855/348266801-0eaaf2c7-a0cf-487c-9d6a-09a58e6a3621.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3OTM1NTM0MjcsIm5iZiI6MTc5MzU1MzEyNywicGF0aCI6Ii83NDc4NTUvMzQ4MjY2ODAxLTBlYWFmMmM3LWEwY2YtNDg3Yy05ZDZhLTA5YTU4ZTZhMzYyMS5wbmc_.4TgGwpDT1rColxiqu9DrM70gQYe7aOL1tz4j6UyiIH8\"><img width=\"1017\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/747855/348266801-0eaaf2c7-a0cf-487c-9d6a-09a58e6a3621.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3OTM1NTM0MjcsIm5iZiI6MTc5MzU1MzEyNywicGF0aCI6Ii83NDc4NTUvMzQ4MjY2ODAxLTBlYWFmMmM3LWEwY2YtNDg3Yy05ZDZhLTA5YTU4ZTZhMzYyMS5wbmc_.4TgGwpDT1rColxiqu9DrM70gQYe7aOL1tz4j6UyiIH8\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">And then I fired up Kitty to see what happens there. It does render the double width icons in <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.files</code>, but <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.tabline</code> oddly renders the <strong>active</strong> tab with the single width icon. As I switch between buffers, the active buffer's icons shrinks. Here is a video:<br>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/17c11b19-921a-45ca-adc4-29d9df8dcbd4\">https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/17c11b19-921a-45ca-adc4-29d9df8dcbd4</a></p>",
    "bodyText": "For those that use mini.files, are your icons using the single width variant instead of the double width variant? I looked in the source code and there is a space appended when the icon is selected, so I'm not sure why my terminal (wezterm) is not rendering the double width icon. As you can see in the screenshot, it does render the double width icon in the tabline, so I'm not really sure what is going on here.\n\nAnd then I fired up Kitty to see what happens there. It does render the double width icons in mini.files, but mini.tabline oddly renders the active tab with the single width icon. As I switch between buffers, the active buffer's icons shrinks. Here is a video:\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/17c11b19-921a-45ca-adc4-29d9df8dcbd4",
